# Backend structure

## Top-level packages (`src/gotit/`)

- `core/` — domain layer, **framework-free** (no `fastapi`/`mcp`/`starlette`
  imports). `core/agents/`, `core/resume/`, `core/loop.py`, `core/models.py`.
- `db/` — SQLAlchemy async adapters: `models.py` (ORM), `session.py`,
  `runtime.py`, and `ops/` (domain operations).
- `api/` — FastAPI: `main.py`, `settings.py`, `auth.py`, `deps.py`,
  `routes/` (route package).
- `mcp/` — MCP tool surface (`server.py`). Thin: calls `db.ops` + `core`,
  never duplicates domain logic.
- `harness/` — dev/gate case sets.
- `prompts/` — prompt loader.

Iron law: **REST and MCP share the same domain operations** (`db.ops`) and
schemas (`core.models`). Never put verification logic in `api/` or `mcp/`.

## `db/ops/` — subdomain modules

One module per subdomain; each owns its rows + view helpers.

| module | owns |
|---|---|
| `_common.py` | constants (`DEFAULT_USER_ID`, `EXCERPT_LEN`) + shared view helpers (`_excerpt`, `_plan_item_view`, `_note_view`, `_claim_view`) |
| `day.py` | learning-day, plan CRUD, due-claims, `fill_today_from_queue`, `get_today`, chat messages |
| `note.py` | notes CRUD, `stub_extract_claim`, `_strip_html`, `ingest_note`, `curate_claims`, note/project claim listing |
| `claim.py` | examine writeback (`apply_examine_result/verdict`), `list_topic_claims_today`, `list_project_claims` |
| `project.py` | project CRUD + `project_progress` |
| `resume.py` | resume upsert/get/apply |
| `drill.py` | drill materials + sessions |
| `prompt.py` | prompt register/get/list |
| `memory.py` | memory add/list |
| `harness.py` | harness run/case persistence |

`__init__.py` is a **barrel** that re-exports every public name (plus
`_strip_html`, used by routes), so callers do `from gotit.db import ops as
day_ops` and never import a submodule directly.

### Circular-import rule

The only cycle is `day ↔ note`. Break it by importing **one direction at
module top** (`day` imports `note.list_notes`) and the reverse via **local
imports inside functions** (`note` locally imports `day.ensure_day`). Any new
cross-subdomain call that would form a cycle must follow this pattern; prefer
pushing the shared primitive into `_common` instead.

## `api/routes/` — one router per subdomain

Each route module declares `router = APIRouter()` and its own Pydantic
request/response models. `routes/__init__.py` aggregates via
`router.include_router(...)` and exposes `router`, so `main.py` keeps
`from gotit.api.routes import router`.

Shared helpers live in `routes/_common.py`: `_user_id`, `_resume_ext`,
`active_prompt`, `_run_sage`, and resume constants shared across modules.

## When adding a feature

1. Pick the subdomain module in `db/ops/` (or add one + barrel re-export).
2. Add the route in the matching `api/routes/` module (or add one + register in
   `__init__`).
3. Add the MCP tool in `mcp/server.py` calling the same `db.ops` function.
4. Keep `core` framework-free; new domain types go in `core/models.py`.
